WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.870
-As President Trump brags
about his handling

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.105
of the hurricane in Puerto Rico,
it's becoming clearer than ever

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.307
that there are no adults
around Trump

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:10.209
to control his worst impulses.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.412
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:16.582
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:19.985
One of the many jobs a President
has is to reassure people

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:22.122
that the government
can handle a crisis.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.923
Trump, of course,
is incapable of that,

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.225
as he demonstrated yesterday
when after a briefing

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.227
on preparations
for Hurricane Florence,

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:29.461
he said this...

00:00:29.461 --> 00:00:33.232 line:0%
-I received a briefing
from Secretary Nielsen,

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:36.035 line:0%
Administrator Long,
and my senior staff

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.270 line:0%
regarding Hurricane Florence.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.773 line:0%
They haven't seen anything like
what's coming at us

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:44.511 line:0%
in 25, 30 years...

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.245 line:0%
maybe ever.

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:49.215 line:0%
It's tremendously big
and tremendously wet.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.550
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.888
-"Tremendously big
and tremendously wet."

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.289
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.291
A deadly storm is bearing down
on our coast

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:02.061
and you're making it sound like
a fancy British water park.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.364
[ British accent ] "Tremendously
big and tremendously wet.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:07.667
You'll have
a splashing good time."

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.669
My favorite thing about that
clip is he literally has

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:13.472
two charts full of information
right next to him.

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.674
All he had to do
is look left or right,

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:18.177
but instead he decided to ramble
off the top of his head

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:22.015
like a fifth grader who just
saw a mall fountain.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.517
"It was tremendously big
and tremendously wet,

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.152
"and I threw a quarter in it

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.220
and wished that I wasn't
President anymore!"

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.755
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.958
With a massive --
with a massive hurricane

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:34.794
bearing down on millions
of people,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.230
it's as important as ever
to have a competent government,

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.998
and yet we have a President
who is not only

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:42.034
dangerously incompetent
but proud of his incompetence.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:43.936
Yesterday, for example,
he called his response

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:47.106
to the hurricane in Puerto Rico
an unsung success

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.242
and today doubled down
on that.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.909 line:0%
-Here's what the President
just posted.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:53.946
He says, "We got A-pluses
for our recent hurricane work

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:56.982
"in Texas and Florida and did
an unappreciated great job

00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:00.486
"in Puerto Rico even though
an inaccessible island

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.522
"with very poor electricity
and a totally competent

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:05.157
"Mayor of San Juan.

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:07.827
We are ready for the big one
that is coming!"

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.829
-First of all, Puerto Rico
is not an inaccessible island.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:12.532
They have a Ritz-Carlton,

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:15.200
and JetBlue has a flight there
every half hour.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.871
You're talking about it like
it's Skull Island.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:21.407
"It's impossible to help them
because their electrical grid

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.776
is constantly being torn up
by Kong."

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.879
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.547
Second, it's not reassuring
when the President talks about

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:32.384
a potentially devastating storm
like he's Fred Sanford.

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:34.921
-Oh! It's the worst one.
This is the big one.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.589
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.589 --> 00:02:39.726
-Seriously.
[ Applause ]

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.729
You're calling a humanitarian
disaster that left thousands

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:46.065
of American citizens dead
an unappreciated success

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.100
while attacking the people
who actually tried to do

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.568
something about it.

00:02:49.568 --> 00:02:52.572
Not only is our President
a callous, incompetent moron,

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:55.208
he's also an ass,
an ass that's...

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.709
-Tremendously big
and tremendously wet.

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:01.214
-Now...
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:04.417
Trump's ability --

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.619
Trump's ability to reassure
the public during a crisis

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.321
has also been made more
difficult by famed journalist

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:12.091
Bob Woodward's new book
"Fear," an insider account

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.460
of the turmoil
in Trump's White House.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.596
The quotes in the Woodward book
are just the latest

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.531
in a parade of anonymous
Trump officials

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.199
who have come forward
to warn the country

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:23.102
that the President is
dangerously unfit for office.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.505
And in response,
Trump has been going on TV

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.506
to convince people
that he's not.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:29.708
At recent events, for example,
he's been carrying around

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:33.245
a printed-out list of what he
claims are his accomplishments.

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:36.349
-An article was just printed,

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.452
just came out
a few minutes ago.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:44.624
"Trump breaks the record
for budget gridlock wins.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.693
Scores big win."

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:50.696
Point after point
after point, if you look.

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:52.431
We've never had period --

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.667
even if you look at the
Olympics, got the Olympics.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.637
The World Cup, just got --
you just saw them.

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:59.605
They were in my office,
got the World Cup.

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:03.342
I have a list,
and the list goes on and on.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.545
It's four pages of things
that the Trump administration

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:07.980
has accomplished.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.849
And if I read it to you --

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.984
Look at this, this is --
if I read --

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:15.487
Each dot is a thing, okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.756
And some of those things are
very big things.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:19.525
-Oh, yeah, yeah. He --

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.995
He definitely just described it
the way it was described to him.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.464
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.064
"Mr. President,
we have a list for you."

00:04:26.064 --> 00:04:28.133
"What the hell is that?
I'm not gonna read that!"

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.003
"You don't have to read it,
just know that, um...

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.306
each dot is a thing."

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:37.343
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.779
"And some of those things
are very big things."

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:42.448
"Oh, cool, cool. Cool."
[ Applause ]

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:46.418
"I'm going to keep this then."

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:48.554
Well, apparently actual voters
haven't had a chance

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.323
to read the dots that are things
yet because according to

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:53.826
a slew of new polls that have
come out in the past week,

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.861
Trump's approval ratings
are taking a nose dive

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:58.430
just as the fall campaign season
gets under way.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:01.967
-CNN's new poll has some really
bad news for President Trump.

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.837
Only 36% of Americans approve

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:07.072
of his handling of his job.

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:09.609
-Eight high quality polls

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.577
have been completed
in the past two weeks,

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.679
and every single one of
them -- look at this --

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.382
has Trump's approval rating
falling.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:19.351 line:0%
-President Trump has the
lowest approval rating

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.487 line:0%
heading into his first
midterm election

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:25.390 line:0%
of any President since 1954.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.793
-That's right, Trump's
approval rating is plummeting.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:30.095
Mr. President, let me explain
it to you this way.

00:05:30.095 --> 00:05:31.597
Each dot is a thing.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.666
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.335
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:37.636
Some of those things
are bad things.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:41.741
Now, maybe voters are getting
tired of hearing the argument

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:44.109
from pundits and Republicans
that Trump's erratic behavior

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:46.112
is tolerable because
there are so-called adults

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.414
in the room who can control
his worst impulses.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.516
It's a line we've heard
repeatedly,

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:53.151
including in that infamous
"New York Times" op-ed.

00:05:53.151 --> 00:05:55.488
-The official writes,
"It may be cold comfort

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:58.524
"in this chaotic era,
but Americans should know

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.859
that there are adults
in the room."

00:06:00.859 --> 00:06:03.696
-I do think that the motivation
was probably to try

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:06.164
to convince voters,
reassure voters

00:06:06.164 --> 00:06:07.866
for the upcoming
midterm elections,

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:09.702
that there are adults
in the room.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.437 line:0%
-You have all of these people
around the President

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.706 line:0%
constantly, over the last
year or so,

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:17.309 line:0%
doing things on their own
to try to stop President Trump.

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:20.980 line:0%
-I would hope the staff over
there would figure out ways

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:22.848 line:0%
of controlling him.

00:06:22.848 --> 00:06:25.985
-He's the President, you
shouldn't have to control him.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:29.321
You're talking about him like he
just escaped from Skull Island.

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:31.557
[ Laughter ]
"He's about to tweet something!

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.993
Quick, shoot him
with a tranquilizer dart."

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.161
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:36.963
So that's been the line
for two years,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.198
responsible people around Trump
are helping him

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:40.899
make good decisions,
especially on issues

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:42.167
like foreign policy
and the military.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.437
People like GOP Senator
Lindsey Graham.

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.472
Graham was once considered
an establishment Republican

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.641
who would rein Trump in,
which is why Republicans

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.342
were heartened to see him
developing a rapport

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:51.811
with the President.

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:53.846
According to Woodward's book,
early in Trump's presidency,

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.581
"Trump invited Graham to
lunch at the White House.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.049
"When he walked into
the Oval Office,

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:58.985
"Trump was sitting
behind the Resolute Desk.

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:01.153
"He jumped up, moved swiftly
toward Graham

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.488
"and gave him a big hug.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.090
"'We got to be friends,'
Trump said.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.858
"'You're going to be
my friend.'

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:09.028
'Yes, sir,' Graham replied.
'I want to be your friend.'"

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:11.630
Oh, my God, insider accounts
of this White House

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.466
read like an episode
of "Dora the Explorer."

00:07:14.466 --> 00:07:17.002
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:19.538
"You're...

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.440
You're going to be my friend."

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.009
"Okay, I'll be your friend."

00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:25.244
"Come on,<i> vámonos.</i>
Everybody, lets go!"

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.746
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:28.146
Apparently, that friendship
has blossomed.

00:07:28.146 --> 00:07:30.183
In fact, when Trump called
Woodward last month

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:32.484
to complain that Woodward hadn't
interviewed him for his book,

00:07:32.484 --> 00:07:34.787
Woodward explained on the call,
which he recorded,

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:38.023
that he'd tried to get through
to Trump by talking to Graham.

00:07:38.023 --> 00:07:39.658
-I certainly don't mind
talking to you,

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:42.161
and I wish I could have
spoken to you.

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:44.897
But, you know, nobody
called my office.

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:47.599
I mean, you went through,
I guess, different people.

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:50.302
-Mr. President, how can I spend
all this time

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:54.339
talking to people and --

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:56.842
like Kellyanne and Raj

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.644
and Republican senators?

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.479
-I mean...
-Who were the senators?

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:02.314
No, they never called me
about it.

00:08:02.314 --> 00:08:04.617
-Senator Graham said
he had talked to you

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:07.252
about talking to me.
Now, is that not true?

00:08:07.252 --> 00:08:09.855
-Uhh, Senator Graham actually
mentioned it quickly

00:08:09.855 --> 00:08:11.691
on one meeting.

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:15.161
And you know, that is true.
That is true.

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:17.396
-I love how easy it is
to checkmate Trump.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.031
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:21.300
Takes, like, two moves tops.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.769
Can you imagine if he ever
sat down with Robert Mueller?

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:25.437
"I didn't collude."
"But you did."

00:08:25.437 --> 00:08:26.939
"No, that's true. That's true."

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.774
[ Laughter and applause ]
"Yeah.

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:31.077
"Now that you mention it.
Yeah."

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:34.680
[ Applause ]

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.715
Yeah, I did."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:36.715 --> 00:08:38.484
So there you go,
no one in Congress is closer

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:40.519
to Trump than Lindsey Graham,
which is why it was terrifying

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.721
to read in Woodward's book
that Graham once pitched Trump

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:45.024
on a bat [bleep] crazy scheme
to assassinate

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:46.825
North Korean leader
Kim Jong-Un.

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.594
"Woodward reports that Graham
tried to solve

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.696
"the Trump administration's
biggest foreign policy dilemma

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:53.499
"by advocating a plan
to murder Kim Jong-Un

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:55.901
"and turn North Korea
into a Chinese colony.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:58.070
"Graham argued, 'China needs to
kill him and replace him

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.805
"'with a North Korean general
they control.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:01.440 line:0%
They need to take him out.'"

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.942
That's insane.

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:05.044
Lindsey Graham wanted Trump
to get the Chinese government

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:07.046
to assassinate Kim Jong-Un.

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:09.015
That sounds like the plot
of a Jack Ryan novel

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:11.250
called "Jack Tryin'
to Get Us All Killed."

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.918
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:14.887
In fact, this is isn't even
first time Graham has tried

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:16.955
to convince Trump to kill
a foreign leader.

00:09:16.955 --> 00:09:20.560
He also urged Trump to kill
Syrian dictator Bashar al-Assad.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.494
Advice Trump apparently
agreed with.

00:09:22.494 --> 00:09:23.795
According to Woodward,
Trump called

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:26.131
Secretary of Defense
James Mattis in 2017

00:09:26.131 --> 00:09:27.399
and pitched the idea.

00:09:27.399 --> 00:09:29.402
Trump told Mattis,
"'Let's [bleep] kill him.

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:32.304
"Let's go in. Let's kill
the [bleep] lot of them.'

00:09:32.304 --> 00:09:34.406
"Mattis told the President that
he would get right on it.

00:09:34.406 --> 00:09:36.809
"But after hanging up the phone,
he told a senior aide,

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.344
'We're not going to do
any of that.'"

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:40.045
[ Laughter ]

00:09:40.045 --> 00:09:43.615
That is how I talk
to my grandpa.

00:09:43.615 --> 00:09:45.785
"What's that, Grandpa?
You want me to come to Florida

00:09:45.785 --> 00:09:47.286
"and set up an Instagram account

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.854
"so you can look at teenagers
in bikinis?

00:09:48.854 --> 00:09:50.222
"Yeah, no, I, uh...

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:51.557
"Yeah, I'm definitely
going to do that.

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:52.691
"I'll see you next week.

00:09:52.691 --> 00:09:54.060
Yeah, I'm not doing
any of that."

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:55.594
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:58.030
Lesson of all this is that there
are no adults in the room.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.733
And even if there were, there's
nothing they could do.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:02.501
The problem begins and ends
with Trump

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:04.036
and the Republicans
supporting him.

00:10:04.036 --> 00:10:06.238
They are actively collaborating
with Trump,

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:08.007
despite the fact
that his brain is...

00:10:08.007 --> 00:10:09.441
-Tremendously wet.

00:10:09.441 --> 00:10:11.610
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:15.348
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

